  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Innovation Fund Healthcare</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cordaid wants to innovate in areas where we want to position ourselves on.
The communal problem addressed by the three innovation projects is the realisation that the health sector worldwide is the fourth sector in ranking of producing environmental wastage, due to elevated levels of waste of organic materials, consumption of medicines and bandages, disposal of chemicals of laboratories and medicines, energy consumption of clinics but even more of supply chains. When it comes to SRHR, we want to innovate with the use of digital tools.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries:
Burundi: patients of the health facilities included in the project.
Uganda: 80 health workers will receive a capacity building training trajectory on climate friendly and smart waste disposal and management.
DRC: Survivors of SGBV.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Get an answer on the following questions: 
1) How can digital tools support health systems in prevention, with a focus on SRHR and SGBV? 

2) How can health systems be instrumental on climate mitigation and adaptation together and which barriers prevent action (Uganda)? 

3) Could certain low-cost, user-friendly applications of digital tools enhance green healthcare and behavior change among health staff?  Or does digitalization lead to another category of waste and energy infrastructure (e.g., phones, tablets, computers, use of electricity, need for data centers)?</narrative>
  </description>
